00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:08.980
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN, TURN</i>

00:00:08.690 --> 00:00:09.360
<b><i>#ENCODERGASM PRESENTS</i></b>

00:00:08.980 --> 00:00:11.900
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN, TURN-A</i>

00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:12.240
<b><i>#ENCODERGASM PRESENTS</i></b>

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:20.240
<i>toki ga mirai ni susumu to dare ga kimeta no da?</i>

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:20.240
<b>Who decided that time should move forward towards the future?</b>

00:00:20.290 --> 00:00:26.830
<i>rakuin o kesu inochi ga rekishi o kakinaosu</i>

00:00:20.290 --> 00:00:26.830
<b>The lives that will erase these brands will rewrite history</b>

00:00:28.250 --> 00:00:34.840
<i>utsukushii tsurugi wa hito to hito tsunagete</i>

00:00:28.250 --> 00:00:34.840
<b>People are connected by beautiful, double-edged swords</b>

00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:44.770
<i>meguri kuru setsuna sa kanashimi wo aratte</i>

00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:44.770
<b>Our coming anticipation will wash away our sadness</b>

00:00:45.810 --> 00:00:53.780
<i>anata to no aida ni inochi aru katachi wo</i>

00:00:45.810 --> 00:00:53.780
<b>With you, between us, life is formed</b>

00:00:53.780 --> 00:01:05.120
<i>Kono hoshi ni sasageru ai to iu shirushi de</i>

00:00:53.780 --> 00:01:05.120
<b>With the proof called "love" that we offer to this planet</b>

00:01:05.710 --> 00:01:06.080
<i>TURN</i>

00:01:06.080 --> 00:01:06.580
<i>TURN-A</i>

00:01:06.580 --> 00:01:07.580
<i>TURN-A TURN,</i>

00:01:07.580 --> 00:01:08.080
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN</i>

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:08.500
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A</i>

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:09.500
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN,</i>

00:01:09.500 --> 00:01:10.210
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN, TURN</i>

00:01:10.210 --> 00:01:13.590
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN, TURN-A</i>

00:01:13.710 --> 00:01:14.090
<i>TURN</i>

00:01:14.090 --> 00:01:14.590
<i>TURN-A</i>

00:01:14.590 --> 00:01:15.590
<i>TURN-A TURN,</i>

00:01:15.590 --> 00:01:16.090
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN</i>

00:01:16.090 --> 00:01:16.510
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A</i>

00:01:16.510 --> 00:01:17.510
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN,</i>

00:01:17.510 --> 00:01:18.180
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN, TURN</i>

00:01:18.180 --> 00:01:20.680
<i>TURN-A TURN, TURN-A TURN, TURN-A</i>

00:01:23.160 --> 00:01:28.650
<i>The Valley of Kingsley was attacked by Dianna Counter because of the spaceship.</i>

00:01:28.650 --> 00:01:30.400
<i>Jacop and Bruno, after joining us...</i>

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:33.730
<i>...fought back with their strange mechanical dolls that we'd never uncovered.</i>

00:01:33.730 --> 00:01:35.900
<i>I now see that they're truly from the Moonrace.</i>

00:01:35.900 --> 00:01:38.530
<i>Despite the tension of the situation...</i>

00:01:38.530 --> 00:01:41.330
<i>Queen Dianna chose to remain here with me...</i>

00:01:41.330 --> 00:01:43.580
<i>And Lieutenant Harry now knows the truth.</i>

00:01:48.960 --> 00:01:53.250
<b>Teteth's Last Words</b>

00:01:53.250 --> 00:01:58.630
This reason we experienced this setback was because someone within our ranks contacted our enemy.

00:01:58.630 --> 00:02:01.220
Treason is quite a thing to throw around.

00:02:01.220 --> 00:02:05.600
As the chief of the Royal Guard, what reason would you have to go to the Militia on your own?

00:02:05.600 --> 00:02:07.940
He was there on an order issued by myself.

00:02:07.940 --> 00:02:09.310
Queen Dianna...

00:02:09.310 --> 00:02:12.310
He was sent to  investigate the spacecraft being excavated by the Militia.

00:02:12.520 --> 00:02:14.820
That should be a job meant for Zenoa's team.

00:02:14.820 --> 00:02:19.320
They have been sent to research the new Mountain Cycle.

00:02:19.320 --> 00:02:22.830
And your task is to deal with the Militia.

00:02:22.830 --> 00:02:26.450
Because of that, I was only able to send the Chief of the Royal Guards, who had no such tasks at the time.

00:02:26.450 --> 00:02:29.030
Well said, Ma'am.

00:02:29.030 --> 00:02:31.040
You're dismissed.

00:02:31.270 --> 00:02:33.130
- That's so awesome!
- I've never seen a vehicle like that!

00:02:33.130 --> 00:02:37.010
- I wanna ride White Doll!
- Why should you get too?
- Why can't I?

00:02:37.010 --> 00:02:39.430
It's been so long since I've had freshly baked bread.

00:02:39.430 --> 00:02:42.000
I knew it'd be a good idea to join the Gallop.

00:02:44.570 --> 00:02:49.430
Why did those people have to come all the way over here? What a pain.

00:02:53.660 --> 00:02:58.440
The way things are now, I'll never complete the plan... My dear Owana.

00:03:02.670 --> 00:03:05.700
Owana, can you see earth?

00:03:05.700 --> 00:03:09.120
Welcome home, Teteth.

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:10.330
Hey, Mama?

00:03:10.330 --> 00:03:11.330
What?

00:03:11.330 --> 00:03:15.840
Why would people who live in a beautiful place like that be barbarians?

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:19.860
Oh? I never guessed I'd see someone like you carrying a doll, Ms. Tate.

00:03:19.860 --> 00:03:21.970
Oh, don't be silly.

00:03:21.970 --> 00:03:25.430
I only have this because it reminds me of an old relic my father gave me ages ago.

00:03:25.430 --> 00:03:27.680
There's nothing strange about it! A girl is allowed to have a doll.

00:03:27.680 --> 00:03:29.930
Troy, stop wasting time here.

00:03:29.930 --> 00:03:32.850
- Get back to helping them move the supplies.
- Forgive me!

00:03:32.850 --> 00:03:35.650
Tate, now would be the time to go and check out the factory.

00:03:35.900 --> 00:03:37.520
Pardon me.

00:03:39.460 --> 00:03:41.900
So now the Militia's using something like that...

00:03:42.590 --> 00:03:45.200
That Mustached Mobile Suit is even more powerful than the SUMO.

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:46.830
It looks that way.

00:03:47.890 --> 00:03:50.830
l didn't guess they'd be bringing you here, Loran.

00:03:50.830 --> 00:03:52.830
Fran didn't come here with you?

00:03:52.830 --> 00:03:57.210
Apparently, she's not interested in an ordinary man who sells bread to both the Militia and Dianna Counter.

00:03:57.210 --> 00:04:02.170
So then is this a neutral territory where the war isn't in effect?

00:04:02.170 --> 00:04:05.720
- Isn't that the daughter of the Heim Family?
- That's right.

00:04:05.720 --> 00:04:08.600
- My name is Keith Laijie.
- I'm Kihel Heim.

00:04:08.600 --> 00:04:10.810
Mr. Keith, I can see that you've been working very hard.

00:04:10.810 --> 00:04:13.940
I'm sure Miss Fran Doll will be able to understand that eventually.

00:04:13.940 --> 00:04:19.280
That's right. Eventually, you'll be able to sell bread to all of Ameria once this war is finally over.

00:04:19.280 --> 00:04:21.810
Yeah. I'm sure that's true.

00:04:27.170 --> 00:04:31.620
That's what I'm saying. If we don't have any missiles, bombs will work just as well.

00:04:31.620 --> 00:04:34.500
Will we be able to tweak the sprockets on this end?

00:04:34.500 --> 00:04:38.340
All you've done was repaint them in a different color scheme.

00:04:38.340 --> 00:04:41.630
Well, Without the proper expertise, one would never be able to upgrade a machine this complicated.

00:04:41.630 --> 00:04:42.920
I suppose you're right.

00:04:42.920 --> 00:04:45.300
What are you up to, Commander Gavane?

00:04:45.300 --> 00:04:47.430
Look and you'll see.

00:04:47.430 --> 00:04:50.010
It looks like you're sewing my cap...

00:04:50.010 --> 00:04:52.430
You'll be able to accept my proposal, right?

00:04:52.430 --> 00:04:55.060
Yes... But that's moving almost too quickly, isn't it?

00:04:55.310 --> 00:04:57.520
These days, everything seems to be happening rather quickly.

00:04:57.520 --> 00:05:01.530
Whether it's our enemy's deployment, or love, or even the end of one's life.

00:05:01.530 --> 00:05:04.360
Because of that, I don't want to be left with any regrets.

00:05:04.610 --> 00:05:06.520
But l...

00:05:06.880 --> 00:05:08.610
Well, that's it.

00:05:11.490 --> 00:05:15.320
I've been watching over our Lady Sochie for some time now.

00:05:15.710 --> 00:05:17.700
I'm sorry!

00:05:19.690 --> 00:05:21.380
Am I interrupting something?

00:05:21.380 --> 00:05:22.630
No.

00:05:22.630 --> 00:05:28.090
We have pilots for both the Borjarnon and Kapool now, but that doesn't mean you should go around tweaking our battle strategies.

00:05:28.300 --> 00:05:31.810
Preparations for launching that surprise attack have been the only thing on my mind...

00:05:31.810 --> 00:05:33.430
So this is the bread from that Donkey Bakery?

00:05:33.430 --> 00:05:37.190
That stuff's bad. They say our enemy buys that bread as well.

00:05:37.440 --> 00:05:39.720
How does that make this bread bad?

00:05:45.380 --> 00:05:47.740
That small pup's a war orphan as well.

00:05:48.550 --> 00:05:51.150
I've already taken several pictures like this one...

00:05:51.150 --> 00:05:55.150
The news honestly needs to find happier things to report about as well.

00:05:55.150 --> 00:05:56.620
That girl?

00:05:56.620 --> 00:05:58.120
Miss Fran Doll...

00:05:58.120 --> 00:06:00.920
Have you seen where Loran went off too?

00:06:00.920 --> 00:06:04.000
I heard he was heading off to investigate something and stopped by the bakery.

00:06:04.000 --> 00:06:06.720
If that's where the Gallop went, my sister must be there too.

00:06:06.720 --> 00:06:08.210
You think so?

00:06:13.280 --> 00:06:15.020
He'll be back soon.

00:06:15.020 --> 00:06:18.220
- Wait for us, Mustache!
- Mustache!

00:06:20.450 --> 00:06:23.600
Was that Mobile Suit really buried here on the Earth?

00:06:24.580 --> 00:06:28.280
That man... he used to be a member of Dianna Counter...

00:06:30.170 --> 00:06:32.320
He's picking bread crumbs up off of the ground and eating 'em!

00:06:32.320 --> 00:06:34.080
I'm gonna go tell Keith's people!

00:06:34.330 --> 00:06:37.120
Every single grain grants us life...

00:06:37.120 --> 00:06:39.110
Every single little grain...

00:06:40.270 --> 00:06:44.000
After you've finished dinner, we're going to start baking the next batch for the others.

00:06:44.000 --> 00:06:47.130
- Alright then!
- We'll be feeding a large battalion of soldiers, right?

00:06:47.130 --> 00:06:48.170
There you are.

00:06:48.170 --> 00:06:53.210
Feel free to drop off your meal here, Ma'am.

00:06:53.990 --> 00:06:55.920
We'll be returning soon.

00:06:55.920 --> 00:07:00.520
Truth be told, the merchants in the town near here have a strong disliking for the Moonrace.

00:07:00.520 --> 00:07:05.020
They'll lie about medical supplies being out of stock, not to mention the title of "traitor" they give these people.

00:07:05.020 --> 00:07:07.740
Why wouldn't they be willing to sell to me?

00:07:07.900 --> 00:07:09.740
Why else do you think?

00:07:09.740 --> 00:07:14.330
There are many rumors that you sell bread to the Moon's army.

00:07:14.330 --> 00:07:18.120
At any rate, I'm not exactly enthusiastic about having to pay a three fold markup.

00:07:18.120 --> 00:07:20.710
Don't you need the baking supplies?

00:07:20.710 --> 00:07:23.210
Give the merchants this message.

00:07:23.210 --> 00:07:27.000
I'm well aware of the 300% profits you've gained from reselling Dianna Counter's medicinal herbs.

00:07:27.000 --> 00:07:29.800
I'm sure I can persuade them to consider giving me a discount.

00:07:29.800 --> 00:07:33.460
That's not going to work, Master Keith.

00:07:33.460 --> 00:07:35.010
This contains your bill.

00:07:35.010 --> 00:07:37.310
Those who have the right intentions will be met with good fortune.

00:07:37.310 --> 00:07:40.560
Then I must be off, Ma'am. I expect to work with you next month as well.

00:07:40.810 --> 00:07:43.270
No, the pleasure was all mine.

00:07:43.270 --> 00:07:45.230
What that? Is it a new car?

00:07:45.400 --> 00:07:47.520
Nope...

00:07:48.250 --> 00:07:49.690
You both seem to be doing well.

00:07:49.900 --> 00:07:53.530
I feel guilty for saying this, but the war has brought us good fortune.

00:07:53.530 --> 00:07:56.620
Perhaps that's why Guin Rhineford seems to be enjoying his war.

00:07:56.620 --> 00:07:58.330
Do you think so?

00:07:58.330 --> 00:08:03.620
I believe his mind is mainly focused on acquiring new technologies.

00:08:03.620 --> 00:08:06.500
Well, isn't that because the war's been spreading?

00:08:06.500 --> 00:08:10.010
Military technology is often like a toy for grown men.

00:08:10.010 --> 00:08:12.880
The only thing that men want to do is play with it.

00:08:13.130 --> 00:08:15.720
A toy for men...

00:08:15.720 --> 00:08:18.250
Something they love to play with...

00:08:18.250 --> 00:08:20.420
I wonder if all men are that way?

00:08:26.290 --> 00:08:28.190
Heavenly girl!

00:08:28.190 --> 00:08:30.030
That's it!

00:08:30.030 --> 00:08:31.530
Ms. Tate, what's the matter?

00:08:31.530 --> 00:08:33.110
I want to collect some alms for the monk.

00:08:33.110 --> 00:08:34.610
Some alms?

00:08:35.260 --> 00:08:36.530
Where are you off to?

00:08:36.530 --> 00:08:38.620
I've seen someone which I believe I can use.

00:08:39.180 --> 00:08:42.620
Okay. I think that we can use this girl named Kihel Heim, as well.

00:08:42.620 --> 00:08:45.330
Heavenly girl...

00:08:45.330 --> 00:08:47.330
The first be enwrapped in string...

00:08:47.330 --> 00:08:49.910
by heaven's special bagworm...

00:08:51.270 --> 00:08:53.010
Help yourself, Mr. Monk.

00:08:53.010 --> 00:08:54.930
I humbly thank you.

00:08:57.570 --> 00:09:00.930
Hey, aren't you the man known as Corin Nander?

00:09:00.930 --> 00:09:03.310
Weren't you a Sergeant?

00:09:03.310 --> 00:09:07.420
The heavenly girl of beauty...

00:09:07.420 --> 00:09:10.520
Hey, could you please help us out once more?

00:09:10.520 --> 00:09:12.820
It could be your chance to earn back your name.

00:09:12.820 --> 00:09:15.020
Perhaps even return to Dianna Counter.

00:09:15.590 --> 00:09:17.910
The great god, White Doll...

00:09:17.910 --> 00:09:19.730
It's back.

00:09:26.770 --> 00:09:28.500
We've arrived at our destination!

00:09:28.500 --> 00:09:30.000
Shut down the engines!

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:31.710
All systems check.

00:09:31.710 --> 00:09:33.410
Check, Complete!

00:09:33.770 --> 00:09:35.510
Welcome back!

00:09:35.510 --> 00:09:37.430
Now, bring in the next load!

00:09:37.430 --> 00:09:39.140
This batch should be for Dianna Counter, right?

00:09:39.140 --> 00:09:41.510
But isn't Michael with the Militia?

00:09:43.810 --> 00:09:47.300
It'd be far too difficult for a single person on her own to steal the Mustache...

00:09:48.160 --> 00:09:50.010
Are you alone?

00:09:50.960 --> 00:09:54.320
It's a beautiful night, isn't it? Could we just...

00:09:54.320 --> 00:09:56.740
It's a shame the moon didn't come out.

00:09:56.740 --> 00:10:01.330
- That's right. The moon's something these people like to stare at, right?
- Indeed.

00:10:01.330 --> 00:10:03.900
If Jacop and Bruno ended up spotting me here...

00:10:06.260 --> 00:10:08.500
What's the matter, Ms. Tate?

00:10:08.500 --> 00:10:10.920
You came down here from the moon, didn't you?

00:10:10.920 --> 00:10:13.130
It's not a place I have fond memories of.

00:10:13.130 --> 00:10:14.920
Oh, I see.

00:10:14.920 --> 00:10:17.750
Sheesh. She'll make love to anybody...

00:10:17.750 --> 00:10:19.560
Don't pull so hard, please.

00:10:19.560 --> 00:10:23.430
After coming to the earth, life here has proven to be pretty difficult for me.

00:10:23.430 --> 00:10:25.520
It was the same way for me.

00:10:25.520 --> 00:10:28.270
So you really are someone who was from the Moonrace...

00:10:28.270 --> 00:10:32.730
Any girl would be happy staying with a nice man like yourself.

00:10:32.730 --> 00:10:34.730
I... I guess so.

00:10:39.170 --> 00:10:41.700
Commander Gavane, huh?

00:10:43.180 --> 00:10:46.240
Loran, please hurry back.

00:11:04.410 --> 00:11:08.430
Alright! This'll be a shot of the Militia's FLAT.

00:11:10.870 --> 00:11:13.640
It'll take about 20 seconds of exposure to take the picture.

00:11:15.370 --> 00:11:19.140
But, after they repainted it, it doesn't really even look like a FLAT anymore.

00:11:24.090 --> 00:11:25.620
Hmm?

00:11:25.620 --> 00:11:27.450
This machine's build...

00:11:27.450 --> 00:11:30.160
Is this the same one that we used two years ago?

00:11:30.970 --> 00:11:33.070
In that case...

00:11:33.070 --> 00:11:36.120
Keith once sat right here in this chair!

00:11:39.770 --> 00:11:42.550
After that, we didn't hear from each other for a full two years...

00:11:42.550 --> 00:11:44.720
Then the war started...

00:11:45.490 --> 00:11:48.930
Keith became a merchant who takes advantage of war...

00:11:48.930 --> 00:11:52.230
Loran became a Militia pilot...

00:11:52.230 --> 00:11:56.220
And I became a reporter who's only paid by commission when I get a good shot.

00:11:59.590 --> 00:12:03.530
What do you think you're doing? Sitting in other people's mobile suits...

00:12:03.530 --> 00:12:05.030
I... I'm sorry.

00:12:05.030 --> 00:12:07.120
Were you the one who spoke with Miss Sochie?

00:12:07.120 --> 00:12:09.240
Right. I'm Fran Doll.

00:12:09.240 --> 00:12:11.120
And you are Mr. Joseph Yaht?

00:12:11.120 --> 00:12:15.420
You were one of the Militia's first pilots who was able to operate a huge mechanical doll.

00:12:15.420 --> 00:12:18.630
Were you the journalist who changed Loran's name to Laura?

00:12:18.630 --> 00:12:20.170
Why did you call him Laura?

00:12:20.420 --> 00:12:22.130
Why? Well, because...

00:12:22.130 --> 00:12:25.550
I thought it would be better if Dianna Counter didn't know who Loran actually was.

00:12:25.550 --> 00:12:29.350
I suppose so. Does that mean you're also from the Moonrace?

00:12:29.350 --> 00:12:34.350
Judging from the fact that you are sitting here, and from the fact that you are Loran's friend...

00:12:34.350 --> 00:12:36.650
...I'm right, aren't I?

00:12:36.650 --> 00:12:39.430
Well, whatever. You're one of the returned populous now.

00:12:40.000 --> 00:12:42.350
I guess you could say that.

00:12:46.470 --> 00:12:48.870
So, has it begun?

00:12:48.870 --> 00:12:51.740
I suppose I'll have to wait until I wake up for the results.

00:13:11.200 --> 00:13:13.140
Is this really alright?

00:13:13.140 --> 00:13:15.230
I could have waited until tomorrow morning.

00:13:15.230 --> 00:13:18.360
After we get the supply of bread tomorrow morning, we'll be leaving right away.

00:13:18.360 --> 00:13:19.730
It's fine.

00:13:19.730 --> 00:13:24.520
In that case, I wanted to move some wheat flour out from the grain storehouse's top floor.

00:13:26.590 --> 00:13:28.740
Alright, please move the hand to the upper entrance.

00:13:28.740 --> 00:13:30.120
- Like this?
- Yes.

00:13:30.120 --> 00:13:31.740
Thanks for your help...

00:13:31.740 --> 00:13:33.330
...Mr. Loran Cehack.

00:13:33.330 --> 00:13:38.630
Forgive me, Mr. Loran... We need the Mustached mechanical doll.

00:13:38.630 --> 00:13:42.050
You... bring all of his stuff over here to me.

00:13:42.050 --> 00:13:44.720
Loran, move the Mustache's hands over toward the cockpit.

00:13:44.720 --> 00:13:47.430
No good can come of this.

00:13:47.430 --> 00:13:50.850
This Mustache machine is one of the infamous "Gundam" types.

00:13:50.850 --> 00:13:52.430
Gundam?

00:13:52.430 --> 00:13:55.850
The marking on its forehead that looks like an upside down A.

00:13:55.850 --> 00:13:58.440
It can also be seen as the symbol "Turn A"

00:13:58.440 --> 00:14:00.520
It should be some bug or error code...

00:14:00.520 --> 00:14:04.070
No, it represents the true code name. It's known as the "Turn A Gundam".

00:14:04.230 --> 00:14:05.820
So why does that matter?

00:14:05.820 --> 00:14:11.620
That monster penned the tragedy of the Dark History. "Gundam", was the nemesis who oppressed the space immigrants!

00:14:11.620 --> 00:14:14.790
Make sure you grab that computer notepad in his bag!

00:14:14.790 --> 00:14:17.250
Uh, Right! Forgive me...

00:14:17.250 --> 00:14:20.040
But then why are you doing something like this, Ms. Teteth?

00:14:20.040 --> 00:14:22.250
If I brought this to the right people in Dianna Counter...

00:14:22.250 --> 00:14:24.840
...I'd gain more than assassinating Dianna ever would have!

00:14:24.840 --> 00:14:28.430
So the real reason you came to earth, was...

00:14:28.430 --> 00:14:32.430
This one, right? It's a high-spec computer pad!

00:14:32.430 --> 00:14:34.060
Good work.

00:14:34.060 --> 00:14:36.220
Now it's time for you to get down, Loran.

00:14:36.220 --> 00:14:38.230
Can you really operate this?

00:14:38.230 --> 00:14:39.730
What's with that goldfish?

00:14:39.730 --> 00:14:41.940
It's just something I bought from a flea-market.

00:14:41.940 --> 00:14:43.820
You really are just a child, aren't you?

00:14:43.820 --> 00:14:45.730
Mr. Troy, hand me the computer.

00:14:45.730 --> 00:14:50.320
Sure. But please understand... Ms. Tate's real self, the person that I know, is actually quite gentle.

00:14:50.320 --> 00:14:53.450
This whole time, she's still had an old stuffed doll held to her chest.

00:14:53.970 --> 00:14:56.150
Don't speak of it so bluntly.

00:14:59.770 --> 00:15:03.080
Ms. Teteth, l understand that you want to do this for the Moonrace's honor...

00:15:03.080 --> 00:15:07.120
...but as long as you're living on earth, none of that matters at all!

00:15:07.690 --> 00:15:09.750
What are you...

00:15:09.750 --> 00:15:12.340
Miss, did you hear that gunshot?

00:15:12.340 --> 00:15:14.430
Can you hear Loran's voice anywhere?

00:15:14.430 --> 00:15:17.670
A bakery worker said something about attempting to use the Mustache.

00:15:17.670 --> 00:15:19.430
So honor's the issue here?

00:15:19.430 --> 00:15:21.650
Mr. Bruno, start the Gallop!

00:15:21.650 --> 00:15:24.220
They're going to try and steal the Mustache's weapons!

00:15:22.700 --> 00:15:24.820
- Ms. Teteth, it won't do you any good!

00:15:24.820 --> 00:15:27.360
Stop this before it's too late!

00:15:27.360 --> 00:15:29.940
If the cockpit hatch is open...

00:15:31.800 --> 00:15:34.150
Shots from beneath me? It's moving?

00:15:37.470 --> 00:15:40.530
The left, move to the left! Are you still asleep?

00:15:44.180 --> 00:15:46.450
Ms. Teteth, Please stop this!

00:15:49.480 --> 00:15:51.930
Let go, you jerk!

00:15:51.930 --> 00:15:53.930
You coward!

00:15:53.930 --> 00:15:55.920
Please put the Lady back down!

00:15:56.700 --> 00:15:58.850
Try anything and I'll choke you, Miss.

00:15:58.850 --> 00:16:00.140
Put me down at once!

00:16:00.140 --> 00:16:02.850
I'll be taking this Dianna look-a-like girl with me!

00:16:05.210 --> 00:16:06.150
It's out of ammo...

00:16:06.150 --> 00:16:07.440
Mr. Jacop!

00:16:07.440 --> 00:16:11.020
Teteth... Your plan's far too noisy...

00:16:11.670 --> 00:16:13.530
You bastard, I was trying to sleep down here!

00:16:13.530 --> 00:16:14.610
Sorry about that.

00:16:15.170 --> 00:16:16.520
Pick me up!

00:16:18.240 --> 00:16:20.740
- Please stop!
- You can't get away!

00:16:25.480 --> 00:16:27.130
Ms. Teteth!

00:16:27.130 --> 00:16:29.130
Open up the hatch, and hand over the weapons!

00:16:29.900 --> 00:16:31.760
- Emergency evasive maneuvers!
- I'm setting it to full speed!

00:16:31.920 --> 00:16:33.920
We'll shake it off!!

00:16:41.370 --> 00:16:43.440
Oh no you don't, Miss.

00:16:43.440 --> 00:16:47.020
Ms. Teteth... are you sure stealing that mechanical doll's a good idea!?

00:16:47.020 --> 00:16:49.230
That must be the man she's using.

00:16:49.230 --> 00:16:51.030
Are you all unharmed?

00:16:51.030 --> 00:16:53.320
You weren't hurt, right, foreman?

00:16:53.320 --> 00:16:54.530
Yeah.

00:16:54.530 --> 00:16:56.620
Boss, it looks like everyone got out alright.

00:16:56.620 --> 00:16:58.620
Really? That's a relief.

00:16:58.620 --> 00:17:00.820
What in the world happened here, foreman?

00:17:04.890 --> 00:17:07.920
Please get out of the White Doll at once, Ms. Teteth!

00:17:07.920 --> 00:17:10.130
- ls that big sis, Teteth?
- I'm through with this nonsense!

00:17:10.130 --> 00:17:12.340
Hand over the Mustache's Shield and Rifle!

00:17:12.340 --> 00:17:14.550
It looks like the person who came and stole the Mustache was, in fact...

00:17:14.720 --> 00:17:16.640
...our big sister...

00:17:16.640 --> 00:17:18.550
What should we do, Jacop?

00:17:18.550 --> 00:17:19.930
We have to help, somehow!

00:17:19.930 --> 00:17:21.350
You can't!

00:17:21.350 --> 00:17:24.140
Should that Mobile Suit fall into the hands of Dianna Counter...

00:17:24.140 --> 00:17:26.230
The earth will be plunged even further into chaos!

00:17:26.230 --> 00:17:30.610
It's because of this same earth that my life was ruined!

00:17:30.610 --> 00:17:31.820
Milady...

00:17:31.820 --> 00:17:34.150
How could you be so cruel, sis?

00:17:34.150 --> 00:17:35.740
Please don't do anything foolish!

00:17:35.740 --> 00:17:39.240
Your not the sort of horrible person who'd do these things!

00:17:39.240 --> 00:17:40.580
What is he saying?

00:17:40.830 --> 00:17:46.450
The only reason this war grew complicated was because that Moonrace boy acquired this machine!

00:17:51.690 --> 00:17:52.750
Foreman!

00:17:52.750 --> 00:17:53.630
Sir?

00:17:53.630 --> 00:17:54.630
Hurry and get it.

00:17:54.630 --> 00:17:55.630
What are you going to do?

00:17:55.630 --> 00:17:57.930
I intend to use the grain storehouse.

00:17:57.930 --> 00:18:01.220
Could you please think of some way to attract Loran's attention?

00:18:01.220 --> 00:18:03.100
I see...

00:18:06.870 --> 00:18:08.350
Please, stop this!

00:18:08.350 --> 00:18:10.730
Can't we just get married and leave things as they are, Ms. Tate!?

00:18:10.730 --> 00:18:14.320
You've only lived on earth for a few months. What could you possibly know?

00:18:14.320 --> 00:18:18.820
You're only causing hardships for yourself because you continually do things like this!

00:18:18.820 --> 00:18:20.870
Why see everything through the Moonrace's hatred?

00:18:21.120 --> 00:18:24.240
Why can't you just accept the ideas of those on the Earth?

00:18:24.240 --> 00:18:29.330
Mother tried to become a Moonrace citizen, but because her ancestors were from the Earth, she suffered horribly!

00:18:29.330 --> 00:18:32.710
An earth woman like yourself could never understand my hatred!

00:18:34.980 --> 00:18:36.340
You want me to ram it?

00:18:36.340 --> 00:18:37.840
Run the Gallop into it...

00:18:37.840 --> 00:18:39.340
What's that?

00:18:39.340 --> 00:18:41.040
That light...

00:18:42.570 --> 00:18:44.220
The grain storehouse?

00:18:44.220 --> 00:18:46.270
Jacop, move us over there.

00:18:46.270 --> 00:18:47.930
We'll beat our sis for sure.

00:18:47.930 --> 00:18:50.340
That's right. The Mustache belongs to us, after all.

00:18:50.340 --> 00:18:53.060
I'm glad to hear it, Mr. Bruno, Mr. Jacop.

00:18:57.590 --> 00:18:59.200
You can't do this!

00:18:59.800 --> 00:19:02.440
If you try to escape, I'll beat you to death!

00:19:02.800 --> 00:19:05.780
l don't want to cause any more trouble for Keith's bakery!

00:19:05.780 --> 00:19:07.330
I'll release the rifle...

00:19:07.330 --> 00:19:09.460
And the shield, as well.

00:19:09.460 --> 00:19:12.830
In exchange, you'll hand over the girl!

00:19:13.180 --> 00:19:18.570
Make it look like the engine's stalling. Once we get near the warehouse, push it to the max!

00:19:18.570 --> 00:19:20.720
Push the engine to max at the warehouse!

00:19:20.720 --> 00:19:22.870
Hovering to maximum power... got it.

00:19:22.870 --> 00:19:24.550
It looks like they got our message.

00:19:24.550 --> 00:19:26.560
Chief, you should move back.

00:19:26.560 --> 00:19:28.140
Be careful.

00:19:28.140 --> 00:19:31.270
You attach the shield by locking it onto the left hand.

00:19:31.270 --> 00:19:33.140
Who is that?

00:19:36.000 --> 00:19:38.150
Make sure to let go of the lady first!

00:19:38.150 --> 00:19:40.730
I'll let her go once I've got the rifle.

00:19:41.380 --> 00:19:43.740
Milady, she didn't crunch anything, did she?

00:19:43.740 --> 00:19:45.530
I'm only a little sore.

00:19:45.970 --> 00:19:48.660
Do you have any idea what you're doing?

00:19:48.890 --> 00:19:51.410
You've got your lady master back now.

00:19:59.270 --> 00:20:00.970
Smoke?

00:20:00.970 --> 00:20:02.970
This isn't flour, is it?

00:20:06.780 --> 00:20:08.890
Don't be afraid!

00:20:09.200 --> 00:20:13.230
If you pray to this angelic figure with a peaceful mind...

00:20:13.230 --> 00:20:17.940
...you'll ascend into heaven to meet the great elm's sapling!

00:20:18.150 --> 00:20:20.570
What's happening to Teteth and that boy?

00:20:20.570 --> 00:20:22.780
Has Ms. Tate come down yet?

00:20:23.300 --> 00:20:25.820
- Don't get in my way!
- Get down!

00:20:32.470 --> 00:20:37.340
You were chosen to be one of the pioneers privileged to first reach earth!

00:20:37.340 --> 00:20:39.920
Even if you were once a lower-class citizen, you're now an Elite!

00:20:39.920 --> 00:20:42.250
Even if that's so!

00:20:50.700 --> 00:20:54.350
Ms. Teteth? Ms. Teteth, what's the matter with you!?

00:20:54.350 --> 00:20:56.100
Ms. Teteth!

00:20:56.790 --> 00:20:59.440
Loran... What's wrong, Loran?

00:21:00.290 --> 00:21:02.850
Her eyes are still open...

00:21:03.290 --> 00:21:05.530
And her mouth is open as well...

00:21:05.530 --> 00:21:07.440
Ms. Teteth is...

00:21:10.180 --> 00:21:12.040
Her forehead...

00:21:15.680 --> 00:21:19.040
What's wrong with Ms. Tate? Did she pass out or something?

00:21:19.600 --> 00:21:23.340
It looks like someone around here is sniping Moonrace citizens that defected.

00:21:23.340 --> 00:21:25.720
You should be careful.

00:21:25.720 --> 00:21:27.550
That's impossible!

00:21:27.550 --> 00:21:33.050
Descend into the sky as a bagworm, off to heaven...

00:21:33.870 --> 00:21:38.980
Long ago, Dianna Soriel's people brought back a few of earth's citizens after they'd completed their research.

00:21:38.980 --> 00:21:42.030
Ms. Tate Halleh's ancestors were among those people.

00:21:42.030 --> 00:21:46.030
Because of this, she was always facing abuse while on the moon.

00:21:46.030 --> 00:21:48.280
...and she hoped to one day join the moon's nobility.

00:21:48.450 --> 00:21:51.240
Why did this have to happen?

00:21:51.470 --> 00:21:54.830
So Dianna Soriel is the cause of this sin as well...

00:21:54.830 --> 00:21:58.570
No, you're wrong. That's not true at all.

00:21:58.570 --> 00:22:02.460
Her Majesty, Dianna Soriel, is a person whom has always shown others hope.

00:22:03.190 --> 00:22:05.550
Better load her body into the truck.

00:22:05.550 --> 00:22:06.840
Keith?

00:22:06.840 --> 00:22:08.640
It's cold down there on the ground.

00:22:08.640 --> 00:22:10.420
I guess that's true.

00:22:14.370 --> 00:22:21.430
Dianna.... My own... sins...

00:22:28.530 --> 00:22:34.540
<b><i>Binetsu ga samenai mama</i></b>

00:22:28.530 --> 00:22:34.540
<b>As if unawoken from a slight fever</b>

00:22:34.540 --> 00:22:40.790
<b><i>Utsumuku shounen no hitomi wa</i></b>

00:22:34.540 --> 00:22:40.790
<b>The eyes of the boy hanging his head</b>

00:22:40.790 --> 00:22:46.510
<b><i>Kokoro no umi mitsumete</i></b>

00:22:40.790 --> 00:22:46.510
<b>Gaze upon the sea of his heart</b>

00:22:46.510 --> 00:22:50.510
<b><i>Shizuka ni hohoenderu</i></b>

00:22:46.510 --> 00:22:50.510
<b>And smile silently</b>

00:22:52.220 --> 00:22:57.020
<b><i>Umare kuru mono kiete yuku mono</i></b>

00:22:52.220 --> 00:22:57.020
<b>What is born, and what fades away</b>

00:22:57.020 --> 00:23:03.230
<b><i>Subete wa sadame no furiko no haba</i></b>

00:22:57.020 --> 00:23:03.230
<b>Are but the sway of the pendulum of fate</b>

00:23:03.230 --> 00:23:08.950
<b><i>Zasetsu no yami o tsukinuke mietekuru</i></b>

00:23:03.230 --> 00:23:08.950
<b>Piercing the darkness of frustration, he begins to see it</b>

00:23:08.950 --> 00:23:14.530
<b><i>Sore ga hikari no shinjitsu</i></b>

00:23:08.950 --> 00:23:14.530
<b>It is the reality of the light</b>

00:23:14.530 --> 00:23:16.870
<b><i>Aura</i></b>

00:23:14.530 --> 00:23:16.870
<b>Aura</b>

00:23:16.870 --> 00:23:25.340
<b><i>Yoake totomoni wasuresareru hoshi ni sasagu</i></b>

00:23:16.870 --> 00:23:25.340
<b>Together with dawn, he gives an offering to the stars that will be forgotten</b>

00:23:25.340 --> 00:23:27.630
<b><i>Aura</i></b>

00:23:25.340 --> 00:23:27.630
<b>Aura</b>

00:23:27.630 --> 00:23:35.510
<b><i>Shijou no ai wa chiisana sono te no naka ni aru</i></b>

00:23:27.630 --> 00:23:35.510
<b>History's love lies in his tiny hands</b>

00:23:40.240 --> 00:23:42.960
<i>Milady Sochie is now suddenly engaged...</i>

00:23:42.960 --> 00:23:45.690
<i>I think she just desperately wants to cling to something secure.</i>

00:23:46.150 --> 00:23:50.190
<i>At the same time, a bizarre fake White Doll suddenly appears.</i>

00:23:50.190 --> 00:23:52.900
<i>This war seems to be going from bad, to worse.</i>

00:23:53.450 --> 00:23:57.160
<i>And as a result, Queen Dianna makes an important decision.</i>

00:23:58.550 --> 00:24:02.780
<i>Next time... on </i>TURN A GUNDAM...
"Laura's Distant Howl"

00:24:03.420 --> 00:24:05.990
"Is there any wind left to blow?"

00:24:03.500 --> 00:24:08.420
<b>Laura's Distant Howl</b>
